// Deliberately carries no EXPECT marker: this is a crash regression test,
// not a language-behaviour test. Minimized by afl-tmin from an AFL++
// campaign against the Contextual Extension work (see cpp/ToDo): a bare,
// nameless Reference Shorthand field ("-> X") with an explicit leading
// ascent segfaulted, because ADLStoreSink::reference_type() (adlstore.h)
// deliberately calls current_context() *before* start_object() has
// resolved frame().handle (needed to look up the reference's target type
// before the field itself exists) - current_context()'s own new
// multi-component/explicit-ascent path dereferenced that still-null
// Handle. Fixed by falling back to the old, stack-based answer whenever
// frame().handle isn't resolved yet, rather than assuming it always is.
// Correctly fails to resolve ("Top object must be called TOP", since
// this isn't wrapped in "TOP {...}") but must not crash.
.->b
